ean_source","scalar.source_finite_adaptive_lower_lean_source","scalar.source_gaussian_column_split_lean_source","scalar.source_predictable_lower_lean_source","scalar_value_comparator","scalar_value_finite_cutoff_antecedent","scalar_value_implementation","scalar_value_type","scope_281","support-r2-13-finite-density-call","support_backward_source","support_certificate_lean_source","support_certificate_source","support_closure_lean_source","support_closure_source","support_coercivity_source","support_contact_lean_source","support_contact_source","support_curvature_source","support_diffusion_source","support_fixed_time_polynomials","support_fixed_time_source","support_flux_source","support_forward_source","support_gap_lean_source","support_model_lean_source","support_model_source","support_optimality_chl","support_regularity_source","support_stieltjes_lean_source","support_tails_source","support_terminal_defect_lean_source","support_terminal_lean_source","support_terminal_source","support_transfer_source","support_uniqueness_lean_source","support_variation_source"],"missing_effective_citation_ids":[]},"passage_citation_audits":[{"anchor":"zero-candidate","effective_required_citation_ids":["authored_r8_support_zero_candidate_descent","full_support_chord_derivative","scalar-r2-26-cite-paper-admissible","support_diffusion_source","support_model_lean_source","support_model_source","support_optimality_chl","support_regularity_source","support_uniqueness_lean_source","support_variation_source"],"missing_effective_citation_ids":[]}],"citation_audit_scope":"Recorded documentary references only; missing effective citation IDs do not establish a mathematical or editorial verdict.","heading_syntax":"ATX headings only; Setext and HTML headings are not parsed","scope":"Mapped passages are correspondences, not sentence-level formal support. Section-passage overlaps are document structure, not claim or proof implications. Unmapped text and passages omitted by the selector remain in the validated paper. Graph records outside the selected prerequisite closure remain in the bundle and are not asserted absent. Argument links combine recorded Lean references, curated support, formalization correspondence and explicit assumptions; their SCCs describe only that mixed recorded reachability. Reading order and platform decomposition are separate."}},"passages":[{"ref":"sha256:93145ef5687bb57439b6b2cb17b3f040069f7144f8a92e8bed7d3d18237af961/papers/expository.md/sha256:479155de953858e60f1454491ccda2215d88a4c2780e686cdfb8422481c62d9c/papers/expository.json/passages/zero-candidate","anchor":"zero-candidate","selected":true,"text":"\n\\Needspace{11\\baselineskip}\n\n### 7.1 Why the zero candidate does not minimise\n\nReturn to the Gaussian value and slope from Section 3. With $\\gamma=0$,\nthe state is $B_t$. Differentiating the slope once more gives\n\n$$\nX_t=B_t,\\qquad\nu_0(t,x)=2F_{\\mathrm G}\\!\\left(\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1-t}}\\right)-1,\n\\qquad\na_0(t,x)=\\sqrt{\\frac2{\\pi(1-t)}}e^{-x^2/(2(1-t))}.\n$$\n\nA Gaussian integral gives\n$\\mathbb E e^{-B_t^2/(1-t)}=\\sqrt{(1-t)/(1+t)}$. Substituting\ninto $q_0'=\\mathbb E[a_0(t,B_t)^2]$ and integrating from zero yields\n\n$$\nq_0'(t)=\\frac2{\\pi\\sqrt{1-t^2}},\\qquad\nq_0(t)=\\frac2\\pi\\arcsin t.\n$$\n\nThis recovers the half-time value $1/3$. It also shows that\n$q_0(t)\\to1$ while $q_0'(t)\\to\\infty$: convergence of a function\nat one does not bound its derivative there.\nThe constant direction $\\eta=1$ is admissible and adds an atom at zero.\nIts cost is\n\n$$\nD\\mathcal P(0)[1]\n=\\frac12\\int_0^1\\left(\\frac2\\pi\\arcsin t-t\\right)dt\n=\\frac14-\\frac1\\pi<0.\n$$\n\nSo a small positive constant coefficient improves the zero candidate.\nThis calculation uses the heat and variation formulas, not a minimiser\nhypothesis; see also [Chen–Handschy–Lerman, proof of Theorem 6][chl-optimality].\n","content_span":{"start_byte":45248,"end_byte":46415,"start_line":1070,"end_line":1108},"block_span":{"start_byte":45217,"end_byte":46447,"start_line":1070,"end_line":1109},"section_ref":"sha256:93145ef5687bb57439b6b2cb17b3f040069f7144f8a92e8bed7d3d18237af961/papers/expository.md/sections/44775","evidence_class":"example","rationale":"Optional complete heat and arcsine computation with an exact negative feasible directional derivative; the elementary half-time example is on the main route. This is an admissible nonminimizer.","claim_ids":["support.regularity","support.diffusion","support.moment_identity","support.first_variation","support.zero_candidate_descent"],"citation_ids":["authored_r8_support_zero_candidate_descent","full_support_chord_derivative","scalar-r2-26-cite-paper-admissible","support_diffusion_source","support_model_lean_source","support_model_source","support_optimality_chl","support_regularity_source","support_uniqueness_lean_source","support_variation_source","support_zero_candidate_chl"],"assumption_ids":["scalar.paper_admissible"],"treatments":[{"claim_id":"support.first_variation","kinds":["application"],"rationale":"Applies the derivative formula to gamma=0 and the feasible constant direction, obtaining a negative cost and hence a nonminimising example. The calculation does not apply a minimiser-only contact or saturation conclusion."},{"claim_id":"support.moment_identity","kinds":["application"],"rationale":"Uses the general moment identity with the explicit heat curvature to calculate q0 prime and q0. The displayed value q0(1/2)=1/3 distinguishes that general identity from the minimiser-only identity q=t."}]}],"correspondence_links":[{"from":"sha256:93145ef5687bb57439b6b2cb17b3f040069f7144f8a92e8bed7d3d18237af961/papers/expository.md/sha256:479155de953858e60f1454491ccda2215d88a4c2780e686cdfb8422481c62d9c/papers/expository.json/passages/zero-candidate","to":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/nodes/support.regularity","kind":"maps_claim","semantic_class":"passage_correspondence","derived":true,"source_ref":"sha256:4